      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T16:40:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with Alice that `#ifdef CONFIG_MEMFD_ASHMEM_SHIM` here is preferable for a couple of reasons:\n1. better documents what we are doing;\n2. avoid extra function call (I think might also be an additional trampoline). Note that even though [1] declares the function as inline, it won\u0027t be inlined because we store the address of this function.\n3. IIUC this is the only place where memfd_ashmem_shim_ioctl() and others are being used. This lets us remove the stubs and additional #ifdefs at [1].",
